\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22\lang9  the configuration for your deployment, including the number of replicas (pods), container images, ports, and any other necessary configurations like environment variables, volumes, etc.\par
\par
deploy the ems-ui application inside a pod and expose it with a service.\par
\par
\cf1\ul\b\fs28 1. Create the Deployment File\par
\cf0\ulnone\fs22 basic deployment.yaml for deploying ems-ui with a service in Kubernetes:\par
\cf2 vim deployment.yaml\par
\cf3 apiVersion: apps/v1\par
kind: Deployment\par
metadata:\par
  name: ems-ui-deployment\par
spec:\par
  replicas: 1  # Number of pod replicas\par
  selector:\par
    matchLabels:\par
      app: ems-ui\par
  template:\par
    metadata:\par
      labels:\par
        app: ems-ui\par
    spec:\par
      containers:\par
      - name: ems-ui\par
        image: lakshmipriyapbt/ems-employee:u1  # Replace with your image name\par
        ports:\par
        - containerPort: 3000  # Port on which the application is running inside the container\par
\par
---\par
apiVersion: v1\par
kind: Service\par
metadata:\par
  name: ems-ui-service\par
spec:\par
  selector:\par
    app: ems-ui  # The service will match pods with this label\par
  ports:\par
    - protocol: TCP\par
      port: 3000  # Port the service will expose on the cluster\par
      targetPort: 3000  # Port on the container that the service will forward traffic to\par
      nodePort: 30401  # External port accessible via the node's IP\par
  type: NodePort  # Expose the service via NodePort (available externally)\par
\cf0\par
\par
What this YAML defines:\par
Deployment:\par
A deployment called ems-ui-deployment is created.\par
The deployment uses a container ems-ui based on the image lakshmipriyapbt/ems-employee:u1 (adjust this image as necessary).\par
The container exposes port 3000.\par
\par
Service:\par
A service called ems-ui-service is created to expose the application.\par
The service exposes port 3000 and forwards traffic to the container's port 3000.\par
The service uses NodePort, and nodePort is set to 30401, making it accessible on the node's IP at port 30401.\par
\par
Explanation of the File:\par
Deployment Section:\par
replicas: 1: This ensures that one instance of the pod is running. You can scale this by changing the number of replicas.\par
matchLabels: It ensures that the deployment matches the pod label (app: ems-ui).\par
containerPort: 3000: The container inside the pod will listen on port 3000, as inferred from your netstat output.\par
image: The container image used for the deployment. Change it to your actual image if it's different.\par
Service Section:\par
This section defines the service that exposes the pod.\par
The port is 3000, which matches the internal port on the container.\par
The nodePort is set to 30401 so that you can access the service externally using {{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK http://<node-ip>:30401 }}{\fldrslt{http://<node-ip>:30401\ul0\cf0}}}}\f0\fs22 .\par
\cf1\ul\fs28\par
2. Deploy the YAML File\par
\cf0\ulnone\b0\fs22 Once you have the deployment.yaml file, apply it to your Kubernetes cluster with kubectl\par
\cf2 kubectl apply -f deployment.yaml\par
\cf0\par
\cf1\ul\b\fs28 3. Verify the Deployment and Service\par
\cf2\ulnone\b0\fs22 kubectl get deployments\par
kubectl get pods\par
kubectl get svc\par

